# What NOT to upload to the API project (see VERCEL.md, Step 1).
#
# This project's root is deployed as-is, so the deny-list matters more than
# usual: db/ is the local MySQL data directory (~350 MB) and backups/ holds
# .sql dumps (~50 MB). Neither is reachable from the function -- the deployed
# API talks to Aiven -- and a serverless bundle is capped at 250 MB unzipped,
# so shipping them would fail the deploy rather than merely waste time.
#
# The frontend is a SEPARATE Vercel project deployed from web/, which is why
# web/ (and its ~500 MB of node_modules) is excluded here too.

# The local database and its dumps -- the deployed API uses Aiven instead.
db
backups

# The frontend: its own project, its own deployment.
web

node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.log

# Secrets. Real environment variables win over .env (see server.py's
# _load_dotenv), so this could not override the platform's values even if it
# were uploaded -- but a bundle is not a place to keep credentials.
.env
.env.local

.git
TODO

# Scraper runtime state and legacy data files. The scrapers themselves are
# uploaded: server.py builds argv paths under scrapers/, and those paths have
# to resolve even though a deployed scrape is dispatched to GitHub Actions.
scrapers/**/.cursor
scrapers/**/*.json
scrapers/**/*.jsonl
scrapers/slack/users

# Documentation: useful in the repo, dead weight in a function bundle.
*.md
